assistant: Subject: Read unit_amount when price is missing
Vendor API version 2026-10-01 renamed the product's `price` field to `unit_amount` without updating its spec. `get_product` only read `p.price`, so for p-1001 it returned `price: null` and no error. The value didn't change: the new recording's `unit_amount` is 1199, which matches the v1 `price` of 1199 US dollars. The handler in `src/tools/get_product.ts` now uses `p.price ?? p.unit_amount ?? null`. Responses from the old 2026-01-01 version still produce exactly the same output as before, and new-version responses get the right price. Typecheck, lint and all tests pass, including the repro test. I only fixed `get_product`; I didn't check whether `search_products` or `get_order` are hit by the same rename.

